From 5d35d21818a4fa3fb186c219329e20383ffbfbfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: el-chan <el-chan@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:54:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dspark: record the target top-k logits in the draft trace

The draft trace held the drafter input and the drafts, but not what the
drafter is fitted against: the target (backbone) logits at each verified
position, i.e. U_k before the Markov bias is added.

sample() now keeps the top-k of the logits it just computed when the trace
is open (default k=32, SPARK3_DSPARK_TRACE_TOPK). logits.topk allocates its
own outputs and reads the logits, so sampling is bit-for-bit unchanged and
with the trace off the capture is a single falsy module-level check: no
copy, no kernel, no allocation. Greedy verification steps never materialise
full-vocabulary logits; they record "lx": 1 instead of "l".

The top-k goes to <path>.topk.f32 / <path>.topk.i32 (raw little-endian,
rows * k per step, so both files share one byte offset); each JSON line
carries its own slice as "l": {"off", "rows", "k"}, where off already
includes the requests row offset from cu_num_logits.
